---
title: Student or teacher?
description: The entry page sends you to the campus if you came to learn, or to the instructor space if you came to teach.
sidebar:
  order: 0
---

`ismos.xyz/entrar` isn't a form — it's a fork in the road. You pick your profile and we take you to the right place. You enter your credentials on the next step, not on that page.

## The two routes

**I'm a student** → takes you to the campus, `campus.ismos.xyz`. There you sign in with [username and password](/en/acceso/iniciar-sesion/), with [GitHub or Google](/en/acceso/login-github-google/), or [as a guest](/en/acceso/acceso-invitado/).

**I'm a teacher** → takes you to the instructor space, where you [create your teacher account](/en/profesores/registro/), fill in your profile and propose a course.

{% aside title="What if I teach and also study?" %}
They're two separate accounts and they don't get in each other's way: the campus one (Moodle) to follow courses, the instructor one (Authentik) to propose them. Take whichever route matches what you're about to do.
{% /aside %}

## If you took the wrong route

No harm done — nothing is created or deleted by taking the wrong route. Go back to `/entrar` and pick the other one. The instructor space also has a **Go to Moodle** button that takes you to the campus without losing anything you've typed.
